Fix bitcast-convert of literals to and from sub-byte types

LiteralBase::BitcastConvert assumed literal buffers hold the packed
device representation, but literals store sub-byte types unpacked (one
element per byte). The ByteSizeOf-based size check was layout-dependent
(rejecting valid sub-byte bitcasts before layout assignment, passing
with mismatched buffer sizes after), and the raw memcpy garbled values
whenever the packing boundary changed, so a u8 constant bitcast to
s4[2] folded to different values than the same bytes fed as a
parameter.

Make the size check bit-accurate and layout-independent (mirroring
shape inference's StorageBitWidth accounting) and convert through the
packed representation with the same PackIntN/UnpackIntN helpers the
transfer manager uses, so folded constants match device results.
Non-sub-byte bitcasts keep the single-memcpy fast path.

Fixes #38964.

Merging this change closes #47149

